  "result": "The fix is in place. Removing the last owner now goes through the same last-owner check as a demotion.\n\n**Cause:** `removeMember` in `src/server/services/member-service.ts` called `assertLastOwnerRetained(orgId, memberId, \"owner\")`. That helper returns early when the next role is `\"owner\"`, so the check never ran for removals. Demotion passes the real target role, so it was still refused.\n\n**Change:**\n- `removeMember` now passes `null` (\"no role at all\") to `assertLastOwnerRetained`.\n- `assertLastOwnerRetained` accepts `Role | null`. The early return for `\"owner\"` is unchanged, and `null` falls through to the owner count.\n- `scripts/manifest-parts/server.ts` has the matching signature string updated.\n\nI have not run the test suite. The existing `refuses to remove the last remaining owner` test in `tests/services/member-service.test.ts` should now pass.",
